# TASK-260715-12zaq5 developer handoff evidence

Status: ready for review.

## Contract and implementation
- TASK-260715-29ws8l remains the authoritative accepted profile/trust contract. The cancelled simultaneous-multiple-approved override and claim were removed.
- SSHProfileSnapshotV1 decoding again rejects more than one active approved identity. Runtime policy construction also rejects a directly constructed policy with multiple active approvals.
- Sequential rotation is modeled as complete generation 7 with one active identity, followed by complete generation 8 with the prior tuple retained as a canonically ordered revoked tombstone and exactly one replacement approval.
- The production macOS composition exposes only the immutable snapshot-backed SSHApprovedHostIdentityPolicy bound to selected libssh2 capabilities; there is no accept-all, first-use acceptance, TOFU auto-accept, or production bypass.
- The libssh2 connect path evaluates raw host-key evidence before credential lookup. First use returns bounded canonical-host, port, reviewed algorithm, SHA-256 fingerprint, and observation-time evidence but cannot create acceptance. Changed, revoked, unsupported, malformed, and canonical-host/port mismatch decisions map to terminal teardown errors with retry only after configuration change.
- Accepted session and credential request values carry verified algorithm/fingerprint and non-secret provenance/timestamps, never raw host-key bytes. Printable evidence, decisions, acceptance, credential requests, and sessions redact sensitive values.

## Ordering evidence
- Sources/ReluxTunnelLibSSH2Adapter/LibSSH2Transport.swift evaluates hostKeyPolicy at the host-decision phase before credentialProvider invocation and before authentication-attempt accounting. Destination channel opens occur only on a ready authenticated transport.
- The live loopback ordering regression covers first use, changed, exact revoked, unsupported adapter algorithm, canonical-host mismatch, and malformed-policy rejection. Every case asserts credential-provider invocation count 0, authentication attempts 0, direct channels 0, and exec channels 0.

